---
import { alsoIncluded } from "@/data/otto";

const chips = ["Simpler", "Give an example", "Quiz me", "Go deeper"];
---

<section id="features" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-28">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
      Everything Otto does, in one quiet notch.
    </h2>
    <p class="reveal mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-otto-muted">
      Each feature follows one rule: help arrives where you are, and it leaves the moment you are done.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-14 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <article class="spotlight reveal group rounded-3xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface p-6 sm:p-8 md:col-span-2">
      <div class="grid-fade relative mb-8 h-44 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-bg">
        <div class="absolute left-1/2 top-4 h-9 w-40 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-black transition-[width,height,border-radius] duration-500 ease-otto group-hover:h-24 group-hover:w-[min(340px,80%)] group-hover:rounded-[20px]">
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">A notch, not a window</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-otto-muted">
        Otto sits at the top edge of your screen. Hover to peek without taking focus, click or press Ctrl+Alt+O to pin it, and collapse mid-answer while the reply keeps streaming.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="spotlight reveal rounded-3xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="grid-fade relative mb-8 h-44 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-bg">
        <div class="snip absolute rounded-md border border-dashed border-otto-text/80 bg-white/[0.04]"></div>
        <div class="absolute bottom-3 left-3 flex gap-1.5">
          <span class="chip-pop rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] text-otto-body" style="--delay: 1.2s">Explain</span>
          <span class="chip-pop rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] text-otto-body" style="--delay: 1.5s">Solve</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Capture only what you point at</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-otto-muted">
        Region snip with scroll stitching for long pages, window and full-screen capture, selected text read through Windows UI Automation, and pasted images. Nothing is captured without your action.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="spotlight reveal rounded-3xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="relative mb-8 h-44 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-bg p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] text-otto-muted">Your draft in another app</p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[13px] text-otto-text"><span class="typer" style="--n: 36">Ice floats because it is less dense.</span></p>
        <span class="absolute bottom-4 left-5 rounded-full bg-otto-sage/15 px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] text-otto-sage">Clipboard untouched</span>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Insert back where you work</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-otto-muted">
        Click Insert on any answer to type clean text at your last focused caret in another app. It never overwrites your clipboard.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="spotlight reveal rounded-3xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="relative mb-8 h-44 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-bg p-5 font-mono text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-otto-body">
        <span class="absolute right-3 top-3 rounded-md bg-white/10 px-2 py-1 font-sans text-[11px] text-otto-text">Copy</span>
        <p><span class="text-otto-lavender">const</span> <span class="text-otto-sage">floats</span> = ice.density &lt; water.density;</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><span class="text-otto-lavender">return</span> <span class="text-otto-amber">true</span>;</p>
        <p class="mt-5 font-sans text-[13px] text-otto-muted">Tables, math, and code render safely.</p>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Answers you can use</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-otto-muted">
        GitHub-flavored tables, KaTeX math, and syntax-highlighted code with a copy button. Raw HTML and scripts never run, and remote images are never fetched.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="spotlight reveal rounded-3xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="relative mb-8 h-44 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-bg p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface px-3 py-2 text-[12px] text-otto-muted">
          Search history: <span class="text-otto-text">derivative</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-[12px]">
          <li class="rounded-md bg-white/[0.08] px-3 py-2 text-otto-text">Derivative, step by step</li>
          <li class="rounded-md px-3 py-2 text-otto-muted">Why does ice float?</li>
          <li class="rounded-md px-3 py-2 text-otto-muted">Lab report, translated</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Searchable local history</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-otto-muted">
        Conversations stay on your PC, with full-text search, rename, delete, and Markdown export. Up to 100 messages per conversation.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="spotlight reveal rounded-3xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface p-6 sm:p-8 md:col-span-2 lg:col-span-3">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Follow-ups that teach</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-otto-muted">
            Retry, edit and re-run a prompt, queue one follow-up while the answer streams, and stop anytime. A stopped answer keeps its partial text, marked Stopped. After each answer, one-click chips offer the next step.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2.5 rounded-2xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-bg p-6">
          {
            chips.map((chip, index) => (
              <span class="chip-pop rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3.5 py-2 text-sm text-otto-body" style={`--delay: ${0.2 + index * 0.15}s`}>
                {chip}
              </span>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="reveal mt-16 rounded-3xl border border-otto-line bg-otto-surface p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Also included</h3>
    <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {
        alsoIncluded.map((item) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-otto-body">
            <span class="mt-2.5 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-otto-sage"></span>
            {item}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
